-- ccc27-s742-conditional-sentence.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, sections 742 to 742.31 (conditional sentence of imprisonment:
-- definitions, imposing, firearm prohibitions, conditions, bodily substances). Sections 742.4 to 742.7 are in `ccc27-s742-4-breach-and-transfer`.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Every top-level name begins with the label of its provision.
-- Answers are `MAYBE BOOLEAN` (or a MAYBE of a type): JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words, NOTHING elsewhere.
-- The designations and specifications of subsections 742.3(6) and (7), and the regulations of 742.3(10), are machinery (NOTES.md, coverage).

§ `Section 742 -- Definitions`

DECLARE `s 742 kind of change` IS ONE OF
    `s 742 a deletion`
    `s 742 an addition`
    `s 742 an alteration that is neither a deletion nor an addition`

-- src:15860 | change, in relation to optional conditions, includes deletions and additions; (modification)
@ref s 742 "change" (src:15860)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 742 kind of change`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742 change, in relation to optional conditions` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 742 a deletion` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 742 an addition` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 742 an alteration that is neither a deletion nor an addition` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "change, in relation to optional conditions, includes deletions and additions"

-- src:15861 | optional conditions means the conditions referred to in subsection 742.3(2); (conditions facultatives)
@ref s 742 "optional conditions" (src:15861)
GIVEN `the condition is one of the conditions referred to in subsection 742.3(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742 optional conditions` MEANS
    IF `the condition is one of the conditions referred to in subsection 742.3(2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "optional conditions means the conditions referred to in subsection 742.3(2)"

-- src:15862 | supervisor means a person designated by the Attorney General, either by name or by title of office, as a supervisor for the purposes of sections 742.1 to 742.7. (agent de surveillance)
@ref s 742 "supervisor" (src:15862)
GIVEN `s 2 Attorney General: the person who designated is the Attorney General for the proceedings` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is designated, either by name or by title of office, as a supervisor for the purposes of sections 742.1 to 742.7` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742 supervisor` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is designated, either by name or by title of office, as a supervisor for the purposes of sections 742.1 to 742.7`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "supervisor means a person designated by the Attorney General, either by name or by title of office, as a supervisor for the purposes of sections 742.1 to 742.7"
        OTHERWISE `s 2 Attorney General: the person who designated is the Attorney General for the proceedings`   -- JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE if the designator was not the Attorney General; NOTHING if section 2 does not cover the case

§ `Section 742.1 -- Imposing of conditional sentence`

-- The facts of one sentence. R2 of the plan: the punishment of the offence as prosecuted comes from the part that owns the offence, so it is an input record.
DECLARE `s 742.1 facts of the sentence` HAS
    `the person is convicted of an offence`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the sentence of imprisonment the court imposes`                         IS AN Imprisonment
    `the court is satisfied that service of the sentence in the community would not endanger the safety of the community`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court is satisfied that service of the sentence in the community would be consistent with the fundamental purpose and principles of sentencing set out in sections 718 to 718.2`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the punishment for the offence as prosecuted`                           IS A Punishment
    `the offence`                                                            IS A `Provision of the Code`
    `the sentence is imposed under paragraph 239(1)(b)`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the mode in which the offence is prosecuted`                            IS A `Mode of proceeding`
    `the offence is of a sexual nature or was committed for a sexual purpose`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offence involves a victim under 18 years of age`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 2 terrorism offence: the offence is one`                              IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 2 criminal organization offence: the offence is one`                  IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN

-- src:15864 | 742.1 If a person is convicted of an offence and the court imposes a sentence of imprisonment of less than two years, the court may, for the purpose of supervising the offender’s behaviour in the community, order that the offender serve the sentence in the community, subject to the conditions imposed under section 742.3, if
@ref s 742.1 (src:15864)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 742.1 facts of the sentence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.1 the court imposes a sentence of imprisonment of less than two years` MEANS
    IF NOT (facts's `the person is convicted of an offence`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a person is convicted of an offence"
    ELSE `the negation of at least two years`
    WHERE
        `the negation of at least two years` MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 742.1 the sentence of imprisonment is at least that many years` (facts's `the sentence of imprisonment the court imposes`) 2
            WHEN JUST atLeast THEN JUST (NOT (atLeast))
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no term, or a term whose days could carry into a month, is stated

-- src:15865 | (a) the court is satisfied that the service of the sentence in the community would not endanger the safety of the community and would be consistent with the fundamental purpose and principles of sentencing set out in sections 718 to 718.2;
@ref s 742.1(a) (src:15865)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 742.1 facts of the sentence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.1(a) the court is satisfied that service of the sentence in the community would not endanger the safety of the community and would be consistent with sections 718 to 718.2` MEANS
    IF facts's `the court is satisfied that service of the sentence in the community would not endanger the safety of the community`
       AND facts's `the court is satisfied that service of the sentence in the community would be consistent with the fundamental purpose and principles of sentencing set out in sections 718 to 718.2`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if (a) the court is satisfied that the service of the sentence in the community would not endanger the safety of the community and would be consistent with the fundamental purpose and principles of sentencing"

-- src:15866 | (b) the offence is not an offence punishable by a minimum term of imprisonment;
@ref s 742.1(b) (src:15866)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 742.1 facts of the sentence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.1(b) the offence is not an offence punishable by a minimum term of imprisonment` MEANS
    IF facts's `the punishment for the offence as prosecuted`'s `minimum imprisonment` EQUALS `no imprisonment is stated`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) the offence is not an offence punishable by a minimum term of imprisonment"

-- src:15867 | (c) the offence is not an offence under any of the following provisions:
-- src:15868 | (i) section 239, for which a sentence is imposed under paragraph 239(1)(b) (attempt to commit murder),
-- src:15869 | (ii) section 269.1 (torture),
-- src:15870 | (ii.1) section 272 (sexual assault with a weapon, threats to a third party or causing bodily harm),
-- src:15871 | (ii.2) section 273 (aggravated sexual assault), or
-- src:15872 | (iii) section 318 (advocating genocide);
@ref s 742.1(c) (src:15867-15872)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 742.1 facts of the sentence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.1(c) the offence is not an offence under any of sections 239 (for which a sentence is imposed under paragraph 239(1)(b)), 269.1, 272, 273 or 318` MEANS
    IF (facts's `the offence`'s `section` EQUALS 239 AND facts's `the sentence is imposed under paragraph 239(1)(b)`)
       OR elem (facts's `the offence`'s `section`) (LIST 269.1, 272, 273, 318)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) the offence is not an offence under any of the following provisions"
    ELSE JUST TRUE   -- the list of excluded provisions is closed by the paragraph itself: an offence outside it meets (c)

-- src:15873 | (c.1) the offence is not an offence, prosecuted by way of indictment, under any of the following provisions:
-- src:15874 | (i) section 153.1 (sexual exploitation of person with disability), or
-- src:15875 | (ii) section 271 (sexual assault);
@ref s 742.1(c.1) (src:15873-15875)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 742.1 facts of the sentence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.1(c.1) the offence is not an offence, prosecuted by way of indictment, under section 153.1 or 271` MEANS
    IF facts's `the mode in which the offence is prosecuted` EQUALS `by indictment` AND elem (facts's `the offence`'s `section`) (LIST 153.1, 271)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c.1) the offence is not an offence, prosecuted by way of indictment, under any of the following provisions"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:15876 | (c.2) the offence is not an offence, prosecuted by way of indictment, of a sexual nature, or committed for a sexual purpose, that involves a victim under 18 years of age; and
@ref s 742.1(c.2) (src:15876)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 742.1 facts of the sentence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.1(c.2) the offence is not an offence, prosecuted by way of indictment, of a sexual nature, or committed for a sexual purpose, that involves a victim under 18 years of age` MEANS
    IF facts's `the mode in which the offence is prosecuted` EQUALS `by indictment`
       AND facts's `the offence is of a sexual nature or was committed for a sexual purpose`
       AND facts's `the offence involves a victim under 18 years of age`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c.2) the offence is not an offence, prosecuted by way of indictment, of a sexual nature, or committed for a sexual purpose, that involves a victim under 18 years of age"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:15877 | (d) the offence is not a terrorism offence, or a criminal organization offence, prosecuted by way of indictment, for which the maximum term of imprisonment is 10 years or more.
@ref s 742.1(d) (src:15877)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 742.1 facts of the sentence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.1(d) the offence is not a terrorism offence, or a criminal organization offence, prosecuted by way of indictment, for which the maximum term of imprisonment is 10 years or more` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF facts's `the mode in which the offence is prosecuted` EQUALS `on summary conviction` THEN JUST TRUE   -- the paragraph speaks only of an offence "prosecuted by way of indictment"
        IF `either s 2 term is JUST TRUE` AND `maximum is ten years or more` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d) the offence is not a terrorism offence, or a criminal organization offence, prosecuted by way of indictment, for which the maximum term of imprisonment is 10 years or more"
        IF `maximum is ten years or more` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `both s 2 terms are JUST FALSE` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): section 2 "terrorism offence" or "criminal organization offence" is not covered on these facts, or no maximum term is stated
    WHERE
        `either s 2 term is JUST TRUE` MEANS
            facts's `s 2 terrorism offence: the offence is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR facts's `s 2 criminal organization offence: the offence is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        `both s 2 terms are JUST FALSE` MEANS
            facts's `s 2 terrorism offence: the offence is one` EQUALS JUST FALSE AND facts's `s 2 criminal organization offence: the offence is one` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        `maximum is ten years or more` MEANS
            `s 742.1 the sentence of imprisonment is at least that many years` (facts's `the punishment for the offence as prosecuted`'s `maximum imprisonment`) 10

-- The whole of section 742.1. The court "may ... if" each condition holds. A grant named "may" whose "if" gate fails answers NOTHING (the ruling of 2026-11-12, fork F-2):
-- the other reading is that a failed condition is the text's own no, JUST FALSE. The paragraph functions above give that "no" paragraph by paragraph.
-- src:15864 | 742.1 If a person is convicted of an offence and the court imposes a sentence of imprisonment of less than two years, the court may, for the purpose of supervising the offender’s behaviour in the community, order that the offender serve the sentence in the community, subject to the conditions imposed under section 742.3, if
-- src:15865 | (a) the court is satisfied that the service of the sentence in the community would not endanger the safety of the community and would be consistent with the fundamental purpose and principles of sentencing set out in sections 718 to 718.2;
-- src:15866 | (b) the offence is not an offence punishable by a minimum term of imprisonment;
-- src:15867 | (c) the offence is not an offence under any of the following provisions:
-- src:15868 | (i) section 239, for which a sentence is imposed under paragraph 239(1)(b) (attempt to commit murder),
-- src:15869 | (ii) section 269.1 (torture),
-- src:15870 | (ii.1) section 272 (sexual assault with a weapon, threats to a third party or causing bodily harm),
-- src:15871 | (ii.2) section 273 (aggravated sexual assault), or
-- src:15872 | (iii) section 318 (advocating genocide);
-- src:15873 | (c.1) the offence is not an offence, prosecuted by way of indictment, under any of the following provisions:
-- src:15874 | (i) section 153.1 (sexual exploitation of person with disability), or
-- src:15875 | (ii) section 271 (sexual assault);
-- src:15876 | (c.2) the offence is not an offence, prosecuted by way of indictment, of a sexual nature, or committed for a sexual purpose, that involves a victim under 18 years of age; and
-- src:15877 | (d) the offence is not a terrorism offence, or a criminal organization offence, prosecuted by way of indictment, for which the maximum term of imprisonment is 10 years or more.
@ref s 742.1 (src:15864-15877)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 742.1 facts of the sentence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.1 the court may order that the offender serve the sentence in the community` MEANS
    IF     (`s 742.1 the court imposes a sentence of imprisonment of less than two years` facts EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       AND (`s 742.1(a) the court is satisfied that service of the sentence in the community would not endanger the safety of the community and would be consistent with sections 718 to 718.2` facts EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       AND (`s 742.1(b) the offence is not an offence punishable by a minimum term of imprisonment` facts EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       AND (`s 742.1(c) the offence is not an offence under any of sections 239 (for which a sentence is imposed under paragraph 239(1)(b)), 269.1, 272, 273 or 318` facts EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       AND (`s 742.1(c.1) the offence is not an offence, prosecuted by way of indictment, under section 153.1 or 271` facts EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       AND (`s 742.1(c.2) the offence is not an offence, prosecuted by way of indictment, of a sexual nature, or committed for a sexual purpose, that involves a victim under 18 years of age` facts EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       AND (`s 742.1(d) the offence is not a terrorism offence, or a criminal organization offence, prosecuted by way of indictment, for which the maximum term of imprisonment is 10 years or more` facts EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court may ... order that the offender serve the sentence in the community ... if (a) ... (d)" (fork F-2: the other reading is JUST FALSE)

§ `Section 742.2 -- Firearm, etc., prohibitions`

