§ `Section 742.3 -- Conditions of a conditional sentence order`

§§ `742.3(1) Compulsory conditions`

DECLARE `s 742.3(1) condition` IS ONE OF
    `s 742.3(1)(a) keep the peace and be of good behaviour`
    `s 742.3(1)(b) appear before the court when required to do so by the court`
    `s 742.3(1)(c)(i) report to a supervisor within two working days, or such longer period as the court directs, after the making of the conditional sentence order`
    `s 742.3(1)(c)(ii) report to a supervisor thereafter, when required by the supervisor and in the manner directed by the supervisor`
    `s 742.3(1)(d) remain within the jurisdiction of the court unless written permission to go outside that jurisdiction is obtained from the court or the supervisor`
    `s 742.3(1)(e) notify the court or the supervisor in advance of any change of name or address, and promptly notify the court or the supervisor of any change of employment or occupation`
    `s 742.3(1) a condition of another kind`

-- src:15885 | 742.3 (1) The court shall prescribe, as conditions of a conditional sentence order, that the offender do all of the following:
-- src:15886 | (a) keep the peace and be of good behaviour;
-- src:15887 | (b) appear before the court when required to do so by the court;
-- src:15888 | (c) report to a supervisor
-- src:15889 | (i) within two working days, or such longer period as the court directs, after the making of the conditional sentence order, and
-- src:15890 | (ii) thereafter, when required by the supervisor and in the manner directed by the supervisor;
-- src:15891 | (d) remain within the jurisdiction of the court unless written permission to go outside that jurisdiction is obtained from the court or the supervisor; and
-- src:15892 | (e) notify the court or the supervisor in advance of any change of name or address, and promptly notify the court or the supervisor of any change of employment or occupation.
@ref s 742.3(1) (src:15885-15892)
GIVEN condition IS A `s 742.3(1) condition`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.3(1) the court shall prescribe the condition as a condition of a conditional sentence order` MEANS
    CONSIDER condition
    WHEN `s 742.3(1)(a) keep the peace and be of good behaviour` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 742.3(1)(b) appear before the court when required to do so by the court` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 742.3(1)(c)(i) report to a supervisor within two working days, or such longer period as the court directs, after the making of the conditional sentence order` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 742.3(1)(c)(ii) report to a supervisor thereafter, when required by the supervisor and in the manner directed by the supervisor` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 742.3(1)(d) remain within the jurisdiction of the court unless written permission to go outside that jurisdiction is obtained from the court or the supervisor` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 742.3(1)(e) notify the court or the supervisor in advance of any change of name or address, and promptly notify the court or the supervisor of any change of employment or occupation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 742.3(1) a condition of another kind` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that the offender do all of the following"

-- (c)(i): the number of working days the text allows is two, or the longer period the court directs. "Working day" is not defined in the text:
-- the count is taken as an input (NOTHING-kind: undefined term, handled by taking the count from the person).
-- src:15888 | (c) report to a supervisor
-- src:15889 | (i) within two working days, or such longer period as the court directs, after the making of the conditional sentence order, and
@ref s 742.3(1)(c)(i) (src:15888-15889)
GIVEN `the working days after the making of the order that passed before the offender reported` IS A NUMBER
      `the longer period the court directed, in working days` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.3(1)(c)(i) the offender reported to a supervisor in time` MEANS
    IF `the working days after the making of the order that passed before the offender reported` AT MOST limit
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within two working days, or such longer period as the court directs" (a period the text fixes in its own words, ruling (a))
    WHERE
        limit MEANS
            CONSIDER `the longer period the court directed, in working days`
            WHEN JUST longer THEN max 2 longer
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 2

DECLARE `s 742.3(1)(c)(i) act` IS ONE OF `s 742.3(1)(c)(i) report to a supervisor`

-- The same duty as a regulative rule. The limit (two working days, or the longer period) is the number the caller passes; the clock counts working days.
-- src:15888 | (c) report to a supervisor
-- src:15889 | (i) within two working days, or such longer period as the court directs, after the making of the conditional sentence order, and
@ref s 742.3(1)(c)(i) (src:15888-15889)
GIVEN limit IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 742.3(1)(c)(i) act`
`s 742.3(1)(c)(i) the offender must report to a supervisor` MEANS
    PARTY `the offender`
    MUST `s 742.3(1)(c)(i) report to a supervisor`
    WITHIN limit
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the offender did not report to a supervisor within two working days, or such longer period as the court directs, after the making of the conditional sentence order"

-- src:15891 | (d) remain within the jurisdiction of the court unless written permission to go outside that jurisdiction is obtained from the court or the supervisor; and
@ref s 742.3(1)(d) (src:15891)
GIVEN `the offender is outside the jurisdiction of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `written permission to go outside that jurisdiction was obtained from the court or the supervisor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.3(1)(d) the offender has complied with the condition to remain within the jurisdiction of the court` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the offender is outside the jurisdiction of the court`)) OR `written permission to go outside that jurisdiction was obtained from the court or the supervisor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "remain within the jurisdiction of the court unless written permission to go outside that jurisdiction is obtained from the court or the supervisor" (fork F-13)

DECLARE `s 742.3(1)(e) change` IS ONE OF
    `s 742.3(1)(e) a change of name`
    `s 742.3(1)(e) a change of address`
    `s 742.3(1)(e) a change of employment`
    `s 742.3(1)(e) a change of occupation`

-- src:15892 | (e) notify the court or the supervisor in advance of any change of name or address, and promptly notify the court or the supervisor of any change of employment or occupation.
@ref s 742.3(1)(e) (src:15892)
GIVEN change IS A `s 742.3(1)(e) change`
      `the court or the supervisor was notified in advance of the change` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court or the supervisor was notified promptly of the change` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.3(1)(e) the offender has complied with the condition to notify of the change` MEANS
    CONSIDER change
    WHEN `s 742.3(1)(e) a change of name` THEN `the advance notice limb`
    WHEN `s 742.3(1)(e) a change of address` THEN `the advance notice limb`
    WHEN `s 742.3(1)(e) a change of employment` THEN `the prompt notice limb`
    WHEN `s 742.3(1)(e) a change of occupation` THEN `the prompt notice limb`
    WHERE
        `the advance notice limb` MEANS
            IF `the court or the supervisor was notified in advance of the change`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "notify the court or the supervisor in advance of any change of name or address" (fork F-14)
        `the prompt notice limb` MEANS
            IF `the court or the supervisor was notified promptly of the change`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "promptly notify the court or the supervisor of any change of employment or occupation" (fork F-14)

§§ `742.3(2) Optional conditions`

DECLARE `s 742.3(2) condition` IS ONE OF
    `s 742.3(2)(a) abstain from the consumption of drugs except in accordance with a medical prescription, of alcohol or of any other intoxicating substance`
    `s 742.3(2)(a.1) provide a sample of a bodily substance on demand`
    `s 742.3(2)(a.2) provide a sample of a bodily substance at regular intervals`
    `s 742.3(2)(a.3) abstain from communicating with a person identified in the order or from going to a place or geographic area specified in the order`
    `s 742.3(2)(b) abstain from owning, possessing or carrying a weapon`
    `s 742.3(2)(c) provide for the support or care of dependants`
    `s 742.3(2)(d) perform community service`
    `s 742.3(2)(e) attend a treatment program approved by the province`
    `s 742.3(2)(f) comply with such other reasonable conditions as the court considers desirable`
    `s 742.3(2) a condition of another kind`

-- src:15897 | (2) The court may prescribe, as additional conditions of a conditional sentence order, that the offender do one or more of the following:
-- src:15898 | (a) abstain from the consumption of drugs except in accordance with a medical prescription, of alcohol or of any other intoxicating substance;
-- src:15899 | (a.1) provide, for the purpose of analysis, a sample of a bodily substance prescribed by regulation on the demand of a peace officer, the supervisor or someone designated under subsection (7) to make a demand, at the place and time and on the day specified by the person making the demand, if that person has reasonable grounds to suspect that the offender has breached a condition of the order that requires them to abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance;
-- src:15900 | (a.2) provide, for the purpose of analysis, a sample of a bodily substance prescribed by regulation at regular intervals that are specified by the supervisor in a notice in Form 51 served on the offender, if a condition of the order requires the offender to abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance;
-- src:15901 | (a.3) abstain from communicating, directly or indirectly, with any victim, witness or other person identified in the order or from going to any place or geographic area specified in the order, except in accordance with any specified conditions that the justice considers necessary;
-- src:15902 | (b) abstain from owning, possessing or carrying a weapon;
-- src:15903 | (c) provide for the support or care of dependants;
-- src:15904 | (d) perform up to 240 hours of community service over a period not exceeding eighteen months;
-- src:15905 | (e) attend a treatment program approved by the province; and
-- src:15906 | (f) comply with such other reasonable conditions as the court considers desirable, subject to any regulations made under subsection 738(2), for securing the good conduct of the offender and for preventing a repetition by the offender of the same offence or the commission of other offences.
@ref s 742.3(2) (src:15897-15906)
GIVEN condition IS A `s 742.3(2) condition`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.3(2) the court may prescribe the condition as an additional condition of a conditional sentence order` MEANS
    CONSIDER condition
    WHEN `s 742.3(2)(a) abstain from the consumption of drugs except in accordance with a medical prescription, of alcohol or of any other intoxicating substance` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 742.3(2)(a.1) provide a sample of a bodily substance on demand` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 742.3(2)(a.2) provide a sample of a bodily substance at regular intervals` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 742.3(2)(a.3) abstain from communicating with a person identified in the order or from going to a place or geographic area specified in the order` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 742.3(2)(b) abstain from owning, possessing or carrying a weapon` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 742.3(2)(c) provide for the support or care of dependants` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 742.3(2)(d) perform community service` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 742.3(2)(e) attend a treatment program approved by the province` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 742.3(2)(f) comply with such other reasonable conditions as the court considers desirable` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 742.3(2) a condition of another kind` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "do one or more of the following"

-- src:15899 | (a.1) provide, for the purpose of analysis, a sample of a bodily substance prescribed by regulation on the demand of a peace officer, the supervisor or someone designated under subsection (7) to make a demand, at the place and time and on the day specified by the person making the demand, if that person has reasonable grounds to suspect that the offender has breached a condition of the order that requires them to abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance;
@ref s 742.3(2)(a.1) (src:15899)
GIVEN `s 2 peace officer: the person making the demand is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person making the demand is the supervisor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person making the demand is designated under subsection (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person making the demand has reasonable grounds to suspect that the offender has breached a condition of the order that requires them to abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.3(2)(a.1) the demand for a sample is within the condition` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person making the demand has reasonable grounds to suspect that the offender has breached a condition of the order that requires them to abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if that person has reasonable grounds to suspect that the offender has breached a condition of the order that requires them to abstain"
        IF `the person making the demand is the supervisor` OR `the person making the demand is designated under subsection (7)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE `s 2 peace officer: the person making the demand is one`   -- a peace officer: JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE if not one ("on the demand of a peace officer, the supervisor or someone designated under subsection (7)"); NOTHING when section 2 does not cover the case

-- src:15900 | (a.2) provide, for the purpose of analysis, a sample of a bodily substance prescribed by regulation at regular intervals that are specified by the supervisor in a notice in Form 51 served on the offender, if a condition of the order requires the offender to abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance;
@ref s 742.3(2)(a.2) (src:15900)
GIVEN `a condition of the order requires the offender to abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the intervals are specified by the supervisor in a notice in Form 51 served on the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.3(2)(a.2) the requirement to provide samples at regular intervals is within the condition` MEANS
    IF `a condition of the order requires the offender to abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance` AND `the intervals are specified by the supervisor in a notice in Form 51 served on the offender`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at regular intervals that are specified by the supervisor in a notice in Form 51 served on the offender, if a condition of the order requires the offender to abstain"

-- src:15904 | (d) perform up to 240 hours of community service over a period not exceeding eighteen months;
@ref s 742.3(2)(d) (src:15904)
GIVEN `the hours of community service` IS A NUMBER
      `the period over which they are to be performed, in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.3(2)(d) the court may prescribe the community service` MEANS
    IF `the hours of community service` AT MOST 240 AND `the period over which they are to be performed, in months` AT MOST 18
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "up to 240 hours of community service over a period not exceeding eighteen months"

-- src:15906 | (f) comply with such other reasonable conditions as the court considers desirable, subject to any regulations made under subsection 738(2), for securing the good conduct of the offender and for preventing a repetition by the offender of the same offence or the commission of other offences.
@ref s 742.3(2)(f) (src:15906)
GIVEN `the condition is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court considers the condition desirable for securing the good conduct of the offender and for preventing a repetition by the offender of the same offence or the commission of other offences` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a regulation made under subsection 738(2) precludes the condition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.3(2)(f) the court may prescribe the other condition` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a regulation made under subsection 738(2) precludes the condition` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "subject to any regulations made under subsection 738(2)"
        IF `the condition is reasonable` AND `the court considers the condition desirable for securing the good conduct of the offender and for preventing a repetition by the offender of the same offence or the commission of other offences` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such other reasonable conditions as the court considers desirable" (a grant named "may": fork F-2: the other reading is JUST FALSE)

§§ `742.3(3) to (9) The court's obligations; samples`

-- src:15908 | (3) A court that makes an order under this section shall
-- src:15909 | (a) cause a copy of the order to be given to the offender and, on request, to the victim;
-- src:15910 | (b) explain the substance of subsection (1) and sections 742.4 and 742.6 to the offender;
-- src:15911 | (c) cause an explanation to be given to the offender of the procedure for applying under section 742.4 for a change to the optional conditions; and
-- src:15912 | (d) take reasonable measures to ensure that the offender understands the order and the explanations.
@ref s 742.3(3) (src:15908-15912)
GIVEN `a copy of the order is given to the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the victim has requested a copy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy is given to the victim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the substance of subsection (1) and sections 742.4 and 742.6 is explained to the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an explanation of the procedure for applying under section 742.4 for a change to the optional conditions is given to the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reasonable measures are taken to ensure that the offender understands the order and the explanations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.3(3) the court has met its obligations on making the order` MEANS
    IF `a copy of the order is given to the offender`
       AND ((NOT (`the victim has requested a copy`)) OR `a copy is given to the victim`)
       AND `the substance of subsection (1) and sections 742.4 and 742.6 is explained to the offender`
       AND `an explanation of the procedure for applying under section 742.4 for a change to the optional conditions is given to the offender`
       AND `reasonable measures are taken to ensure that the offender understands the order and the explanations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A court that makes an order under this section shall (a) ... (b) ... (c) ... and (d) ..." (fork F-14)

-- src:15914 | (4) For greater certainty, a failure to comply with subsection (3) does not affect the validity of the order.
@ref s 742.3(4) (src:15914)
GIVEN `the failure is a failure to comply with subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.3(4) a failure to comply with subsection (3) affects the validity of the order` MEANS
    IF `the failure is a failure to comply with subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a failure to comply with subsection (3) does not affect the validity of the order"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a failure to comply with subsection (3)"

-- src:15916 | (5) The notice referred to in paragraph (2)(a.2) must specify the places and times at which and the days on which the offender must provide samples of a bodily substance under a condition described in that paragraph. The first sample may not be taken earlier than 24 hours after the offender is served with the notice, and subsequent samples must be taken at regular intervals of at least seven days.
@ref s 742.3(5) (src:15916)
GIVEN `the notice specifies the places and times at which and the days on which the offender must provide samples` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the hours between service of the notice and the first sample` IS A NUMBER
      `the intervals between the later samples are regular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shortest interval between samples, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.3(5) the notice and the schedule of samples meet the limits of subsection (5)` MEANS
    IF `the notice specifies the places and times at which and the days on which the offender must provide samples`
       AND `the hours between service of the notice and the first sample` AT LEAST 24
       AND `the intervals between the later samples are regular`
       AND `the shortest interval between samples, in days` AT LEAST 7
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must specify the places and times ... The first sample may not be taken earlier than 24 hours after the offender is served with the notice, and subsequent samples must be taken at regular intervals of at least seven days" (fork F-14)

-- src:15930 | (8) Samples of bodily substances referred to in paragraphs (2)(a.1) and (a.2) may not be taken, analyzed, stored, handled or destroyed, and the records of the results of the analysis of the samples may not be protected or destroyed, except in accordance with the designations and specifications made under subsection (6).
@ref s 742.3(8) (src:15930)
GIVEN `the sample or record is dealt with in accordance with the designations and specifications made under subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.3(8) the taking, analysis, storage, handling or destruction of the sample, or the protection or destruction of the record, is within the designations and specifications` MEANS
    IF `the sample or record is dealt with in accordance with the designations and specifications made under subsection (6)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not be taken, analyzed, stored, handled or destroyed ... except in accordance with the designations and specifications made under subsection (6)" (fork F-13)

-- src:15932 | (9) The Attorney General of a province or the minister of justice of a territory, or a person authorized by the Attorney General or minister, shall cause all samples of bodily substances provided under a conditional sentence order to be destroyed within the periods prescribed by regulation, unless the samples are reasonably expected to be used as evidence in proceedings under section 742.6.
@ref s 742.3(9) (src:15932)
GIVEN `the samples are reasonably expected to be used as evidence in proceedings under section 742.6` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.3(9) the Attorney General or minister of justice shall cause the samples to be destroyed within the periods prescribed by regulation` MEANS
    IF `the samples are reasonably expected to be used as evidence in proceedings under section 742.6`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the samples are reasonably expected to be used as evidence in proceedings under section 742.6" (fork F-13)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 742.31 -- Bodily substances: prohibitions and offence`

-- src:15940 | 742.31 (1) No person shall use a bodily substance provided under a conditional sentence order except for the purpose of determining whether an offender is complying with a condition of the order that they abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance.
@ref s 742.31(1) (src:15940)
GIVEN `the use is for the purpose of determining whether an offender is complying with a condition of the order that they abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.31(1) the use of a bodily substance provided under a conditional sentence order is barred` MEANS
    IF `the use is for the purpose of determining whether an offender is complying with a condition of the order that they abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except for the purpose of determining whether an offender is complying with a condition of the order that they abstain from the consumption of drugs, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance" (fork F-13)
    ELSE JUST TRUE   -- "No person shall use a bodily substance provided under a conditional sentence order"

DECLARE `s 742.31(2) use or disclosure` IS ONE OF
    `s 742.31(3) disclosure to the offender to whom the results relate`
    `s 742.31(3) use or disclosure in the course of proceedings under section 742.6`
    `s 742.31(3) use or disclosure, if the results are made anonymous, for statistical or other research purposes`
    `s 742.31(2) any other use or disclosure, or allowing the disclosure`

-- src:15942 | (2) Subject to subsection (3), no person shall use, disclose or allow the disclosure of the results of the analysis of a bodily substance provided under a conditional sentence order.
@ref s 742.31(2) (src:15942)
GIVEN use IS A `s 742.31(2) use or disclosure`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.31(2) the use or disclosure of the results of the analysis of a bodily substance is barred` MEANS
    CONSIDER use
    WHEN `s 742.31(3) disclosure to the offender to whom the results relate` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsection (3), no person shall use, disclose or allow the disclosure" (fork F-13)
    WHEN `s 742.31(3) use or disclosure in the course of proceedings under section 742.6` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsection (3)" (fork F-13)
    WHEN `s 742.31(3) use or disclosure, if the results are made anonymous, for statistical or other research purposes` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsection (3)" (fork F-13)
    WHEN `s 742.31(2) any other use or disclosure, or allowing the disclosure` THEN JUST TRUE

-- src:15944 | (3) The results of the analysis of a bodily substance provided under a conditional sentence order may be disclosed to the offender to whom they relate, and may also be used or disclosed in the course of proceedings under section 742.6 or, if the results are made anonymous, for statistical or other research purposes.
@ref s 742.31(3) (src:15944)
GIVEN use IS A `s 742.31(2) use or disclosure`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.31(3) the results of the analysis of a bodily substance may be used or disclosed` MEANS
    CONSIDER use
    WHEN `s 742.31(3) disclosure to the offender to whom the results relate` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 742.31(3) use or disclosure in the course of proceedings under section 742.6` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 742.31(3) use or disclosure, if the results are made anonymous, for statistical or other research purposes` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 742.31(2) any other use or disclosure, or allowing the disclosure` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be disclosed to the offender ... and may also be used or disclosed in the course of proceedings under section 742.6 or, if the results are made anonymous, for statistical or other research purposes" (subsection (3) says nothing of other uses; subsection (2) bars them)

-- src:15946 | (4) Every person who contravenes subsection (1) or (2) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 742.31(4) (src:15946)
GIVEN `the person contravenes subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 742.31(4) the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` MEANS
    IF `the person contravenes subsection (1) or (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every person who contravenes subsection (1) or (2) is guilty of an offence" (a failed relative clause read as the text's no: fork F-7)

-- The punishment limb. The text gives the mode, "punishable on summary conviction", and no maximum: section 787 (Part XXVII, not in this range) sets the general maximum.
-- src:15946 | (4) Every person who contravenes subsection (1) or (2) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 742.31(4) (src:15946)
`s 742.31(4) the punishment` MEANS Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`
